# Codex Orchestrator Workflow

Read and follow the repository-root [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). It is the source
of truth for the shared implementation and validation policy.

- Codex must not run post-modification formatters, linters, static type checkers,
  or tests unless the user explicitly asks it to. This includes check-only modes,
  autofixes, targeted tests, and equivalent commands through wrappers or hooks.
- `codex-orchestrator` checks the starting checkout before phase implementation;
  baseline maintenance is separate from phase repairs. After each turn it runs
  prerequisites, then formatting and all independent checks, collecting failures
  together. A failed prerequisite stops the run without spending a repair turn.
- Repair only regressions caused by the assigned phase and its affected contracts.
  Return `blocked` for failures requiring unrelated or explicitly excluded work.
  Return control without rerunning checks or invoking the orchestrator yourself.
- Implementation and repair model choices come from the exported orchestrator
  environment variables documented in `AGENTS.md`. Repairs may switch models while
  retaining the phase session; do not edit Codex configuration to change models.
- Continue writing required tests and reviewing code, tests, documentation, and
  diffs by inspection. Do not weaken tests or checks to hide failures.
- Report checks as deferred, not passed. Outside an orchestrated run, leave their
  execution to the user unless explicitly asked to run them.
- General completion checklists in other rules, plans, or the README do not
  require Codex to execute checks. Apply the validation policy in `AGENTS.md`.
